  "servings": 4,
  "summary": "Highlighting traditional Thai preservation methods, these <b>fermented pork skewers</b> deliver an extraordinary combination of tangy sourness and smoky sweetness. Built around authentic <b>Naem sausage</b>, a cured pork product fermented with sticky rice and garlic, each bite offers a punchy umami profile that transforms when exposed to high heat. Threaded onto bamboo sticks alongside whole shallots and Thai chilies, the meat is brushed with a sticky palm sugar and fish sauce glaze that caramelizes over open coals. The high heat of the grill crisp-chars the exterior while keeping the center succulent and complexly seasoned. This dish represents street food culture at its finest, offering bold dynamic contrasts between sour cured pork and sweet aromatic glaze. Serve these sizzling hot skewers with <b>sticky rice</b>, crisp raw cabbage wedges, and roasted peanuts for an authentic taste of Southeast Asian culinary tradition.",
